/-!
# Cohomology on the complement of a zero locus: the Čech cone model is sheaf cohomology

Let `A` be a commutative ring, let `I` be an ideal generated by a finite family `f₁, …, f_r`
and let `U = Spec A ∖ V(I)`. The formal-functions results of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/ComplementFormalFunctions.lean` and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/ComplementFormalFunctionsHigher.lean` are stated for
`Stacks.Algebraization.complementCohomologyFunctor`, the cohomology of the cone of the Čech
augmentation `C^•(f₁, …, f_r; M) ⟶ M`. This file identifies that functor, **naturally in the
module `M`**, with the sheaf cohomology `H^p(U, M̃|U)` of [Stacks, Tag 01E3] on the open subscheme
`U`, read as an abelian group:

`H^p(U, M̃|U) ≅ H^p(cone(C^•(f; M) ⟶ M))`  for every `p ≥ 0`.

## The chain of identifications

In degree zero both sides are the sections of `M̃` on `U`: on the left by
`HzeroIso` (left exactness of sections), on the right by the degree-zero comparison carried by
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.cechLocalizationTriangleData`, which is natural in the module.

In a degree `p = q + 1 ≥ 1` the comparison is a composite of natural isomorphisms:

1. cohomology on the open subscheme `U` is cohomology over the open `U` of `Spec A`
   (Stacks 01E1, `AlgebraicGeometry.cohomologyOverNatIsoRestriction`);
2. the abelian-group-valued cohomology is the module-valued right derived functor of sections
   (`Stacks.Cohomology.ModuleComparison.rightDerivedEvaluationForgetIso`), which is the cohomology
   of the bounded-below derived sections
   (`Stacks.Cohomology.HigherDirectImagePresheaf.derivedPlusToStandard`);
3. the canonical map from Čech cohomology of the standard covering `U = ⋃ D(f_i)` to cohomology
   (Stacks 01EQ) is an isomorphism at every `M̃`, because the finite intersections of the `D(f_i)`
   are affine (Stacks 01ET and Serre vanishing);
4. the Čech complex of the covering computes the same cohomology as its alternating subcomplex
   (Stacks 01FM), and the alternating Čech complex of `M̃` is the extended Čech complex
   `C^•(f₁, …, f_r; M)` shifted by one;
5. the connecting map of the cone triangle identifies `H^{q+2}(C^•(f; M))` with the degree-`q+1`
   cohomology of the cone.

Each step was available in the library for a single module; what is added here is its naturality
in the module, which is what transports maps (and hence inverse limits along the reductions
`M ⟶ M/fⁿM`) from one model to the other.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Algebraization.ComplementSheafComparison.hfunctorComplementTildeIso`: the natural
  isomorphism `H^p(U, (-)~|U) ≅ complementCohomologyFunctor f p`, as functors from `A`-modules to
  abelian groups.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01E3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01E3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01EQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01EQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ET](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ET)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01FM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01FM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DWR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DWR)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry Stacks.Cohomology.HigherDirectImage

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] ModuleCat.hasLimitsOfSize
attribute [local instance] AddCommGrpCat.hasLimitsOfSize

universe u

/-! ### The slice model of the Čech complex is natural in the sheaf -/

namespace Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf

open Stacks.CategoryTheory.CechComplex
open Stacks.Cohomology.Basis (res res_app)

attribute [local implicit_reducible] CechCochains.Cochain
attribute [local implicit_reducible] Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf.cechComplex

variable {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X]
  {R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u}}
  {ι : Type u}
  (V : Opens X) (U : ι → Opens X) (hU : V = ⨆ i, U i) {I J : SheafOfModules.{u} R}

/-- Taking components of a cochain of the slice model is natural in the sheaf of modules. -/
theorem toCochainFun_map_eq_cochainMap (φ : I ⟶ J) {n : ℕ}
    (s : ToType (((cechComplexFunctor (coverObject U hU)).obj (sectionsPresheaf V I)).X n)) :
    toCochainFun V U hU J
        (ConcreteCategory.hom (((cechComplexFunctorOfCover V U hU).map φ).f n) s) =
      Stacks.Cech.cochainMap (X := TopCat.of X) U ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).map φ).hom n
        (toCochainFun V U hU I s) := by
  funext x
  have hraw : rawcomp V U hU J
      (ConcreteCategory.hom (((cechComplexFunctorOfCover V U hU).map φ).f n) s) x =
      ConcreteCategory.hom (((SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).map φ).hom.app _)
        (rawcomp V U hU I s x) :=
    ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
      (cech_map_comp_π (coverObject U hU) ((sectionsPresheafFunctor V).map φ) n x) s
  refine (congrArg (fun y => res (abSections J) _ (res (abSections J) _ y)) hraw).trans ?_
  rw [res_app, res_app]
  rfl

/-- The inclusion of the alternating Čech complex into the slice model is natural in the sheaf
of modules. -/
theorem alternatingCechInclusionToAbCechComplex_naturality (φ : I ⟶ J) [LinearOrder ι] :
    Stacks.Cech.alternatingCechMap (X := TopCat.of X) U ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).map φ).hom ≫
        alternatingCechInclusionToAbCechComplex V U hU J =
      alternatingCechInclusionToAbCechComplex V U hU I ≫
        ((forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} (SectionRing R V)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapHomologicalComplex
          (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).map ((cechComplexFunctorOfCover V U hU).map φ :
            cechComplex.{u, u, u, u} V U hU I ⟶ cechComplex.{u, u, u, u} V U hU J) := by
  refine HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun n => ?_
  rw [← Iso.cancel_iso_hom_right _ _ (asIso (toCochain V U hU J n)), asIso_hom]
  have hinv : ∀ (K : SheafOfModules.{u} R) (y : CechCochains.Cochain (X := TopCat.of X) U
      (abSections K) n), toCochainFun V U hU K
        (ConcreteCategory.hom ((abCechComplexIso V U hU K).inv.f n) y) = y := fun K y =>
    ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
      (HomologicalComplex.congr_hom (abCechComplexIso V U hU K).inv_hom_id n) y
  ext s
  change toCochainFun V U hU J (ConcreteCategory.hom ((abCechComplexIso V U hU J).inv.f n) _) =
    toCochainFun V U hU J (ConcreteCategory.hom (((cechComplexFunctorOfCover V U hU).map φ).f n)
      (ConcreteCategory.hom ((abCechComplexIso V U hU I).inv.f n) s.1))
  rw [hinv, toCochainFun_map_eq_cochainMap, hinv]
  rfl

/-- Forgetting the module structure commutes with taking cohomology, naturally in the complex. -/
theorem homologyMap_mapHomologicalComplex_comp_mapHomologyIso_hom {S : Type u} [Ring S]
    {K L : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} S) ℕ} (ψ : K ⟶ L) (p : ℕ) :
    HomologicalComplex.homologyMap
        (((forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} S) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapHomologicalComplex
          (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).map ψ) p ≫
        ((L.sc p).mapHomologyIso (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} S) AddCommGrpCat.{u})).hom =
      ((K.sc p).mapHomologyIso (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} S) AddCommGrpCat.{u})).hom ≫
        (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} S) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ψ p) :=
  ShortComplex.mapHomologyIso_hom_naturality
    ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor _ (ComplexShape.up ℕ) p).map ψ)
    (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} S) AddCommGrpCat.{u})

/-- **The comparison of the alternating Čech complex with the slice model is natural in the
sheaf.** -/
theorem alternatingCechHomologyIso_naturality [LinearOrder ι] (φ : I ⟶ J) (p : ℕ) :
    HomologicalComplex.homologyMap (Stacks.Cech.alternatingCechMap (X := TopCat.of X) U
        ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).map φ).hom) p ≫
        (alternatingCechHomologyIso V U hU J p).hom =
      (alternatingCechHomologyIso V U hU I p).hom ≫
        (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} (SectionRing R V)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map
          (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ((cechComplexFunctorOfCover V U hU).map φ :
            cechComplex.{u, u, u, u} V U hU I ⟶ cechComplex.{u, u, u, u} V U hU J) p) := by
  have hc := congrArg (fun ψ ↦ HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ψ p)
    (alternatingCechInclusionToAbCechComplex_naturality V U hU φ)
  simp only [HomologicalComplex.homologyMap_comp] at hc
  have h2' := homologyMap_mapHomologicalComplex_comp_mapHomologyIso_hom
    (K := cechComplex.{u, u, u, u} V U hU I) (L := cechComplex.{u, u, u, u} V U hU J)
    ((cechComplexFunctorOfCover V U hU).map φ) p
  refine ((reassoc_of% hc) _).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
  refine (congrArg (fun t ↦ t ≫ (homologyForgetIso V U hU J p).hom)
    (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap_comp _ _ p)).trans ?_
  refine (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans ?_
  exact whisker_eq _ h2'

end Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf

/-! ### The alternating Čech complex of the standard covering is natural in the module -/

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (fam : Fin r → A) {M N : ModuleCat.{u} A}

/-- The identification of the sections of `M̃` over an intersection of standard opens with a
Čech localization of `M` is natural in the module. -/
theorem cechStandardTupleSectionsEquiv_naturality (g : M ⟶ N) {p : ℕ}
    (σ : Fin p → ULift.{u} (Fin r))
    (y : moduleSections M (CechCochains.inter (cechStandardOpen fam) σ)) :
    cechStandardTupleSectionsEquiv fam N σ (moduleSectionsMap g _ y) =
      cechModMap fam g _ (cechStandardTupleSectionsEquiv fam M σ y) :=
  cechSectionsEquiv_moduleSectionsMap fam g (cechTupleIndices ULift.down σ)
    (moduleSectionsCongr M (inter_eq_cechBasicOpen fam ULift.down
      (cechStandardOpen_eq_basicOpen fam) σ) y)

/-- The degreewise comparison of the ordered Čech cochains of the standard covering with the
terms of `C^•(f₁, …, f_r; M)` is natural in the module. -/
theorem ordCochainToCechTerm_naturality (g : M ⟶ N) (p : ℕ) (s : (orderedCechStandard fam M).X p) :
    ordCochainToCechTerm fam N p (fun σ => moduleSectionsMap g _ (s σ)) =
      cechTermMap fam g (p + 1) (ordCochainToCechTerm fam M p s) := by
  simp only [ordCochainToCechTerm, map_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun σ _ => ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (cechTermMap_lof fam g (p + 1) _ _).symm
  exact congrArg _ (cechStandardTupleSectionsEquiv_naturality fam g σ.1 (s σ))

/-- The degreewise comparison of the alternating Čech complex of the standard covering with the
extended Čech complex shifted by one. -/
def alternatingCechXIso (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (p : ℕ) :
    (Stacks.Cech.alternatingCechComplex (cechStandardOpen fam) (associatedAbPresheaf M)).X p ≅
      (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
        ((_root_.Cech.cechComplex fam (M : Type u)).X (p + 1)) :=
  (HomologicalComplex.eval _ _ p).mapIso
      (Stacks.Cech.orderedIsoAlternatingCechComplex (cechStandardOpen fam)
        (associatedAbPresheaf M)).symm ≪≫ ordCechXIso fam M p

/-- `Stacks.LocalCohomology.alternatingCechXIso` commutes with the differentials. -/
theorem alternatingCechXIso_comm (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (p : ℕ) :
    (alternatingCechXIso fam M p).hom ≫
        (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map
          ((_root_.Cech.cechComplex fam (M : Type u)).d (p + 1) (p + 2)) =
      (Stacks.Cech.alternatingCechComplex (cechStandardOpen fam) (associatedAbPresheaf M)).d
          p (p + 1) ≫ (alternatingCechXIso fam M (p + 1)).hom := by
  simp only [alternatingCechXIso, Iso.trans_hom, Functor.mapIso_hom, Category.assoc,
    ordCechXIso_comm, HomologicalComplex.eval_map]
  rw [← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc]
  congr 1
  exact (Stacks.Cech.orderedIsoAlternatingCechComplex (cechStandardOpen fam)
    (associatedAbPresheaf M)).inv.comm p (p + 1)

/-- `Stacks.LocalCohomology.alternatingCechXIso` is natural in the module. -/
theorem alternatingCechXIso_naturality (g : M ⟶ N) (p : ℕ) :
    (Stacks.Cech.alternatingCechMap (cechStandardOpen fam) (associatedAbPresheafMap g)).f p ≫
        (alternatingCechXIso fam N p).hom =
      (alternatingCechXIso fam M p).hom ≫
        (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map ((cechComplexMap fam g).f (p + 1)) := by
  ext s
  exact ordCochainToCechTerm_naturality fam g p _

end Stacks.LocalCohomology

namespace Stacks.Algebraization.ComplementSheafComparison

open Stacks.LocalCohomology Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf Stacks.Cohomology.CechDerived

/-! ### The cone side: cohomology of the Čech cone is shifted Čech cohomology -/

section Cone

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (fam : Fin r → A)

/-- The triangle `C^•(f; M) ⟶ M ⟶ cone ⟶ C^•(f; M)[1]` of the Čech augmentation, in the derived
category. -/
abbrev coneTriangle [HasDerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)] (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) :
    Triangle (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) :=
  DerivedCategory.Q.mapTriangle.obj
    (CochainComplex.mappingCone.triangle (extendedCechAugmentation.{u} fam M))

/-- The cone triangle is distinguished. -/
theorem coneTriangle_distinguished [HasDerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)] (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) :
    coneTriangle fam M ∈ distTriang _ :=
  DerivedCategory.mappingCone_triangle_distinguished _

/-- A module map induces a morphism of cone triangles. -/
def coneTriangleMap [HasDerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)] {M N : ModuleCat.{u} A} (g : M ⟶ N) :
    coneTriangle fam M ⟶ coneTriangle fam N :=
  DerivedCategory.Q.mapTriangle.map
    (CochainComplex.mappingCone.triangleMap (extendedCechAugmentation.{u} fam M)
      (extendedCechAugmentation.{u} fam N) (extendedCechComplexMap.{u} fam g)
      ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).map g)
      (extendedCechAugmentation_naturality.{u} fam g).symm)

/-- The third component of `coneTriangleMap` is the map of cones. -/
theorem coneTriangleMap_hom₃ {M N : ModuleCat.{u} A} (g : M ⟶ N) :
    (coneTriangleMap fam g).hom₃ = (cechComplementFunctor.{u} fam).map g := rfl

/-- The first component of `coneTriangleMap` is the map of Čech complexes. -/
theorem coneTriangleMap_hom₁ [HasDerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)] {M N : ModuleCat.{u} A}
    (g : M ⟶ N) :
    (coneTriangleMap fam g).hom₁ = DerivedCategory.Q.map (extendedCechComplexMap.{u} fam g) := rfl

/-- The module `M` placed in degree zero has no cohomology outside degree zero. -/
theorem isZero_homology_coneTriangle_obj₂ [HasDerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)]
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (n : ℤ) (hn : n ≠ 0) :
    IsZero ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) n).obj (coneTriangle fam M).obj₂) :=
  IsZero.of_iso (HomologicalComplex.isZero_single_obj_homology _ _ _ _ hn)
    ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors (ModuleCat.{u} A) n).app _)

/-- Above degree zero the connecting map of the cone triangle is an isomorphism. -/
theorem isIso_δ_coneTriangle [HasDerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)] (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (n : ℤ)
    (hn : 1 ≤ n) :
    IsIso (DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.δ (coneTriangle fam M) n (n + 1) rfl) := by
  have hT := coneTriangle_distinguished fam M
  have hmono : Mono (DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.δ (coneTriangle fam M) n (n + 1) rfl) :=
    (DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.exact₃ _ hT n (n + 1) rfl).mono_g
      ((isZero_homology_coneTriangle_obj₂ fam M n (by omega)).eq_of_src _ 0)
  have hepi : Epi (DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.δ (coneTriangle fam M) n (n + 1) rfl) :=
    (DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.exact₁ _ hT n (n + 1) rfl).epi_f
      ((isZero_homology_coneTriangle_obj₂ fam M (n + 1) (by omega)).eq_of_tgt _ 0)
  exact isIso_of_mono_of_epi _

/-- cone cohomology in degree q+1 is Čech cohomology in degree q+2, naturally. -/
def complementCohomologyIsoCechHomology (q : ℕ) :
    complementCohomologyFunctor fam ((q : ℤ) + 1) ≅
      cechFunctor.{u} fam ⋙ HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor _ _ (q + 2) :=
  NatIso.ofComponents
    (fun M ↦ @asIso _ _ _ _ (DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.δ (coneTriangle fam M) _ _ rfl)
        (isIso_δ_coneTriangle fam M _ (by omega)) ≪≫
      (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors (ModuleCat.{u} A) _).app _ ≪≫
      HomologicalComplex.extendHomologyIso _ ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat
        (by change ((q + 2 : ℕ) : ℤ) = (q : ℤ) + 1 + 1; push_cast; ring))
    (fun {M N} g ↦ by
      have h2 := (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors (ModuleCat.{u} A)
        ((q : ℤ) + 1 + 1)).hom.naturality (extendedCechComplexMap.{u} fam g)
      have h3 := HomologicalComplex.extendHomologyIso_hom_naturality (cechComplexMap.{u} fam g)
        ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat (j := q + 2) (j' := (q : ℤ) + 1 + 1)
        (by change ((q + 2 : ℕ) : ℤ) = (q : ℤ) + 1 + 1; push_cast; ring)
      simp only [Functor.comp_map] at h2
      have h1' : (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) ((q : ℤ) + 1)).map
            (coneTriangleMap fam g).hom₃ ≫
          DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.δ (coneTriangle fam N) _ ((q : ℤ) + 1 + 1) rfl =
          DerivedCategory.HomologySequence.δ (coneTriangle fam M) _ ((q : ℤ) + 1 + 1) rfl ≫
            (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) ((q : ℤ) + 1 + 1)).map
              (coneTriangleMap fam g).hom₁ :=
        (Stacks.HomologyLinear.homologySequenceδ_naturality (coneTriangleMap fam g)
          ((q : ℤ) + 1) ((q : ℤ) + 1 + 1) rfl).symm
      refine ((reassoc_of% h1') _).trans ?_
      refine Eq.trans ?_ (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
      refine congrArg (_ ≫ ·) ?_
      refine ((reassoc_of% h2) _).trans ?_
      refine Eq.trans ?_ (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
      exact congrArg (_ ≫ ·) h3)

end Cone

/-! ### The sheaf side: sheaf cohomology on `U` is the Čech cohomology of the standard covering -/

/-- Stacks 01E1 as a natural isomorphism. -/
def hfunctorRestrictNatIso (X : Scheme.{u}) (V : X.Opens) (n : ℕ) :
    Hfunctor X.ringCatSheaf V n ≅
      Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor V.ι ⋙ Hfunctor (V : Scheme).ringCatSheaf ⊤ n := by
  rw [Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SchemeHigherDirectImage.restrictFunctor_eq_moduleRestriction]
  exact AlgebraicGeometry.cohomologyOverNatIsoRestriction (asRingSheafedSpace X.toRingedSpace) V n

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (fam : Fin r → A) (I : Ideal A)
  (hIf : Ideal.span (Set.range fam) = I)

variable (A) in
/-- The associated sheaf `M ↦ M̃` on `Spec A`, as a functor, with `associatedSheaf A M` as its
object part. -/
def associatedSheafFunctor : ModuleCat.{u} A ⥤ (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules where
  obj M := associatedSheaf A M
  map g := (tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of A)).map g
  map_id M := (tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of A)).map_id M
  map_comp g h := (tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of A)).map_comp g h

variable (A) in
/-- `associatedSheafFunctor` is Mathlib's `tilde.functor`. -/
def associatedSheafFunctorIso : associatedSheafFunctor A ≅ tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of A) :=
  Iso.refl _

/-- **Stacks 01E1 for `U = Spec A ∖ V(I)`.** Cohomology of `M̃|U` on the open subscheme `U`
is cohomology of `M̃` over the open `U` of `Spec A`, naturally in the module. -/
def hfunctorComplementTildeIsoSpec (p : ℕ) :
    complementTildeFunctor A I ⋙ Hfunctor (complementZeroLocus A I : Scheme).ringCatSheaf ⊤ p ≅
      associatedSheafFunctor A ⋙
        Hfunctor (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf (complementZeroLocus A I) p :=
  Functor.associator _ _ _ ≪≫ Functor.isoWhiskerLeft _
    (hfunctorRestrictNatIso (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) (complementZeroLocus A I) p).symm ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerRight (associatedSheafFunctorIso A).symm _

/-- The abelian-group-valued cohomology over `U` is the module-valued right derived functor of
sections over `U`. -/
def hfunctorIsoRightDerivedEvaluation (p : ℕ) :
    Hfunctor (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf (complementZeroLocus A I) p ≅
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf
          (op (complementZeroLocus A I))).rightDerived p ⋙ forget₂ _ AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  (Stacks.Cohomology.ModuleComparison.rightDerivedEvaluationForgetIso
      (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf (complementZeroLocus A I) p).symm

/-- The classical right derived functors of sections over `U` are the cohomology of the
bounded-below derived functor. -/
def rightDerivedEvaluationIsoRightDerivedPlus (p : ℕ) :
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf
          (op (complementZeroLocus A I))).rightDerived p ⋙ forget₂ _ AddCommGrpCat.{u} ≅
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf
          (op (complementZeroLocus A I))).rightDerivedPlus (p : ℤ) ⋙ forget₂ _ AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  Functor.isoWhiskerRight
      (Stacks.Cohomology.HigherDirectImagePresheaf.derivedPlusToStandard
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf
          (op (complementZeroLocus A I))) p).symm _

/-- The cohomology of the bounded-below derived functor of sections over `U` is the cohomology
of `Stacks.Cohomology.CechDerived.derivedGlobalSectionsFunctor`. -/
def rightDerivedPlusIsoDerivedGlobalSections (p : ℕ) :
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf
          (op (complementZeroLocus A I))).rightDerivedPlus (p : ℤ) ≅
      Stacks.Cohomology.CechDerived.derivedGlobalSectionsFunctor
          (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf (complementZeroLocus A I) ⋙
          DerivedCategory.Plus.homologyFunctor _ (p : ℤ) := by
  unfold Functor.rightDerivedPlus Stacks.Cohomology.CechDerived.derivedGlobalSectionsFunctor
  exact (Functor.associator _ _ _).symm

/-- **Stacks 01EQ and 01ET for the standard covering.** The canonical map from Čech cohomology
of the covering of `U` by the `D(f_i)` to cohomology is an isomorphism at every `M̃`, naturally in
`M`. -/
def cechCohomologyNatIsoCohomology (p : ℕ) :
    associatedSheafFunctor A ⋙
        (Stacks.Cohomology.CechDerived.cechComplexPlusFunctor
          (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen fam)
          (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen fam I hIf) ⋙
        DerivedCategory.Plus.Q ⋙ DerivedCategory.Plus.homologyFunctor _ (p : ℤ)) ≅
      associatedSheafFunctor A ⋙
        (Stacks.Cohomology.CechDerived.derivedGlobalSectionsFunctor
          (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf (complementZeroLocus A I) ⋙
          DerivedCategory.Plus.homologyFunctor _ (p : ℤ)) :=
  @asIso _ _ _ _ (Functor.whiskerLeft (associatedSheafFunctor A)
    (Stacks.Cohomology.CechDerived.cechCohomologyToCohomology
      (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen fam)
      (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen fam I hIf) (p : ℤ)))
    (@NatIso.isIso_of_isIso_app _ _ _ _ _ _ _
      fun M ↦ (cechCohomologyIsoCohomology fam I hIf M p).isIso_hom)

/-- The Čech cohomology of the covering, read in the bounded-below derived category, is the
homology of the Čech complex of Stacks 01EP, naturally in the module. -/
def cechPlusHomologyNatIso (p : ℕ) :
    associatedSheafFunctor A ⋙
        (Stacks.Cohomology.CechDerived.cechComplexPlusFunctor
          (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen fam)
          (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen fam I hIf) ⋙
        DerivedCategory.Plus.Q ⋙ DerivedCategory.Plus.homologyFunctor _ (p : ℤ)) ≅
      associatedSheafFunctor A ⋙
        (cechComplexFunctorOfCover.{u, u, u} (R := (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf)
          (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen fam)
          (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen fam I hIf) ⋙
          HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor _ _ p) :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (fun M ↦ cechPlusHomologyIso (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen fam)
      (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen fam I hIf) ((associatedSheafFunctor A).obj M) p)
    (fun {M N} g ↦ by
      have h2 := (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors
        (ModuleCat.{u} (SectionRing (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf
          (complementZeroLocus A I))) (p : ℤ)).hom.naturality
        (HomologicalComplex.extendMap ((cechComplexFunctorOfCover.{u, u, u}
          (R := (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf) (complementZeroLocus A I)
          (cechStandardOpen fam) (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen fam I hIf)).map
            ((associatedSheafFunctor A).map g)) ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat)
      have h3 := HomologicalComplex.extendHomologyIso_hom_naturality
        ((cechComplexFunctorOfCover.{u, u, u}
          (R := (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf) (complementZeroLocus A I)
          (cechStandardOpen fam) (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen fam I hIf)).map
            ((associatedSheafFunctor A).map g)) ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat
        (j := p) (j' := (p : ℤ)) rfl
      exact ((reassoc_of% h2) _).trans (congrArg (_ ≫ ·) h3))



/-! ### From the slice model to the alternating Čech complex -/

/-- The alternating Čech complex of the standard covering of `U` with coefficients in `M̃`, as a
functor of the module. -/
abbrev alternatingCechFunctor : ModuleCat.{u} A ⥤ CochainComplex AddCommGrpCat.{u} ℕ :=
  associatedSheafFunctor A ⋙ SheafOfModules.toSheaf (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf ⋙
    sheafToPresheaf _ _ ⋙ Stacks.Cech.alternatingCechComplexFunctor (cechStandardOpen fam)

/-- **The Čech cohomology of the slice model is the cohomology of the alternating Čech
complex, naturally in the module.** -/
def sliceHomologyIsoAlternating (p : ℕ) :
    (associatedSheafFunctor A ⋙
        (cechComplexFunctorOfCover.{u, u, u} (R := (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf)
          (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen fam)
          (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen fam I hIf) ⋙
          HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor _ _ p)) ⋙ forget₂ _ AddCommGrpCat.{u} ≅
      alternatingCechFunctor fam ⋙ HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor _ _ p :=
  (NatIso.ofComponents (fun M ↦ Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf.alternatingCechHomologyIso
      (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen fam)
      (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen fam I hIf) (associatedSheaf A M) p)
    (fun g ↦ alternatingCechHomologyIso_naturality (complementZeroLocus A I)
      (cechStandardOpen fam) (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen fam I hIf)
      ((associatedSheafFunctor A).map g) p)).symm

/-! ### From the alternating Čech complex to the extended Čech complex -/

/-- The degreewise comparison of the alternating Čech complex with the extended Čech complex,
shifted by one. -/
def alternatingXIso (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (p : ℕ) :
    ((alternatingCechFunctor fam).obj M).X p ≅
      (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
        ((_root_.Cech.cechComplex fam (M : Type u)).X (p + 1)) :=
  alternatingCechXIso fam M p

/-- `alternatingXIso` commutes with the differentials. -/
theorem alternatingXIso_comm (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (p : ℕ) :
    (alternatingXIso fam M p).hom ≫
        (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map
          ((_root_.Cech.cechComplex fam (M : Type u)).d (p + 1) (p + 2)) =
      ((alternatingCechFunctor fam).obj M).d p (p + 1) ≫ (alternatingXIso fam M (p + 1)).hom :=
  alternatingCechXIso_comm fam M p

/-- `alternatingXIso` is natural in the module. -/
theorem alternatingXIso_naturality {M N : ModuleCat.{u} A} (g : M ⟶ N) (p : ℕ) :
    ((alternatingCechFunctor fam).map g).f p ≫ (alternatingXIso fam N p).hom =
      (alternatingXIso fam M p).hom ≫
        (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map ((cechComplexMap fam g).f (p + 1)) := by
  ext s
  exact ordCochainToCechTerm_naturality fam g p _

/-- The cohomology of a complex computed through `sc'` is natural. -/
theorem homologyMap_comp_homologyIsoSc'_hom {C : Type*} [Category C] [Limits.HasZeroMorphisms C]
    [CategoryWithHomology C] {ι : Type*} {c : ComplexShape ι} {K L : HomologicalComplex C c}
    (φ : K ⟶ L) (i j k : ι) (hi : c.prev j = i) (hk : c.next j = k) :
    HomologicalComplex.homologyMap φ j ≫ (L.homologyIsoSc' i j k hi hk).hom =
      (K.homologyIsoSc' i j k hi hk).hom ≫
        ShortComplex.homologyMap ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor' C c i j k).map φ) := by
  change ShortComplex.homologyMap ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor C c j).map φ) ≫
      ShortComplex.homologyMap ((HomologicalComplex.natIsoSc' C c i j k hi hk).hom.app L) =
    ShortComplex.homologyMap ((HomologicalComplex.natIsoSc' C c i j k hi hk).hom.app K) ≫
      ShortComplex.homologyMap ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor' C c i j k).map φ)
  rw [← ShortComplex.homologyMap_comp, ← ShortComplex.homologyMap_comp, NatTrans.naturality]

/-- The comparison of the three-term truncations around degree `q + 1` of the alternating Čech
complex and around degree `q + 2` of the extended Čech complex. -/
def alternatingScIso (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (q : ℕ) :
    (HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor' AddCommGrpCat.{u} (ComplexShape.up ℕ) q (q + 1)
        (q + 2)).obj ((alternatingCechFunctor fam).obj M) ≅
      (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapShortComplex.obj
        ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor' (ModuleCat.{u} A) (ComplexShape.up ℕ) (q + 1)
          (q + 2) (q + 3)).obj (_root_.Cech.cechComplex fam (M : Type u))) :=
  ShortComplex.isoMk (alternatingXIso fam M q) (alternatingXIso fam M (q + 1))
    (alternatingXIso fam M (q + 2)) (alternatingXIso_comm fam M q)
    (alternatingXIso_comm fam M (q + 1))

/-- `alternatingScIso` is natural in the module. -/
theorem alternatingScIso_naturality {M N : ModuleCat.{u} A} (g : M ⟶ N) (q : ℕ) :
    (HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor' AddCommGrpCat.{u} (ComplexShape.up ℕ) q (q + 1)
        (q + 2)).map ((alternatingCechFunctor fam).map g) ≫ (alternatingScIso fam N q).hom =
      (alternatingScIso fam M q).hom ≫
        (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapShortComplex.map
          ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor' (ModuleCat.{u} A) (ComplexShape.up ℕ) (q + 1)
            (q + 2) (q + 3)).map (cechComplexMap fam g)) :=
  ShortComplex.hom_ext _ _ (alternatingXIso_naturality fam g q)
    (alternatingXIso_naturality fam g (q + 1)) (alternatingXIso_naturality fam g (q + 2))

/-- In degree `q + 1` the cohomology of the alternating Čech complex of the standard covering
with coefficients in `M̃` is the degree-`q + 2` cohomology of `C^•(f₁, …, f_r; M)`. -/
def alternatingHomologyIso (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (q : ℕ) :
    ((alternatingCechFunctor fam).obj M).homology (q + 1) ≅
      (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
        ((_root_.Cech.cechComplex fam (M : Type u)).homology (q + 2)) :=
  ((alternatingCechFunctor fam).obj M).homologyIsoSc' q (q + 1) (q + 2) (by simp) (by simp) ≪≫
    ShortComplex.homologyMapIso (alternatingScIso fam M q) ≪≫
    ShortComplex.mapHomologyIso ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor' (ModuleCat.{u} A)
      (ComplexShape.up ℕ) (q + 1) (q + 2) (q + 3)).obj (_root_.Cech.cechComplex fam (M : Type u)))
      (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}) ≪≫
    (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapIso
      ((_root_.Cech.cechComplex fam (M : Type u)).homologyIsoSc' (q + 1) (q + 2) (q + 3)
        (by simp) (by simp)).symm

/-- `alternatingHomologyIso` is natural in the module. -/
theorem alternatingHomologyIso_naturality {M N : ModuleCat.{u} A} (g : M ⟶ N) (q : ℕ) :
    HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ((alternatingCechFunctor fam).map g) (q + 1) ≫
        (alternatingHomologyIso fam N q).hom =
      (alternatingHomologyIso fam M q).hom ≫
        (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map
          (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap (cechComplexMap fam g) (q + 2)) := by
  have h1 := homologyMap_comp_homologyIsoSc'_hom ((alternatingCechFunctor fam).map g)
    q (q + 1) (q + 2) (by simp) (by simp)
  have h2 : ShortComplex.homologyMap
        ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor' AddCommGrpCat.{u} (ComplexShape.up ℕ) q (q + 1)
          (q + 2)).map ((alternatingCechFunctor fam).map g)) ≫
        ShortComplex.homologyMap (alternatingScIso fam N q).hom =
      ShortComplex.homologyMap (alternatingScIso fam M q).hom ≫
        ShortComplex.homologyMap ((forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapShortComplex.map
          ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor' (ModuleCat.{u} A) (ComplexShape.up ℕ) (q + 1)
            (q + 2) (q + 3)).map (cechComplexMap fam g))) := by
    rw [← ShortComplex.homologyMap_comp, ← ShortComplex.homologyMap_comp,
      alternatingScIso_naturality]
  have h3 := ShortComplex.mapHomologyIso_hom_naturality
    ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor' (ModuleCat.{u} A) (ComplexShape.up ℕ) (q + 1)
      (q + 2) (q + 3)).map (cechComplexMap fam g))
    (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u})
  have h4 := homologyMap_comp_homologyIsoSc'_hom (cechComplexMap fam g)
    (q + 1) (q + 2) (q + 3) (by simp) (by simp)
  have h5 : ShortComplex.homologyMap
      ((HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor' (ModuleCat.{u} A) (ComplexShape.up ℕ) (q + 1)
        (q + 2) (q + 3)).map (cechComplexMap fam g)) ≫
      ((_root_.Cech.cechComplex fam (N : Type u)).homologyIsoSc' (q + 1) (q + 2) (q + 3)
        (by simp) (by simp)).inv =
      ((_root_.Cech.cechComplex fam (M : Type u)).homologyIsoSc' (q + 1) (q + 2) (q + 3)
        (by simp) (by simp)).inv ≫
      HomologicalComplex.homologyMap (cechComplexMap fam g) (q + 2) := by
    refine (Iso.comp_inv_eq _).2 ?_
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (_ ≫ ·) h4).symm
    exact (Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc _ _).symm
  have h6 := ((forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map_comp _ _).symm.trans
    ((congrArg (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map h5).trans
      ((forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map_comp _ _))
  refine ((reassoc_of% h1) _).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
  refine congrArg (_ ≫ ·) ?_
  refine ((reassoc_of% h2) _).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
  refine congrArg (_ ≫ ·) ?_
  refine ((reassoc_of% h3) _).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
  exact congrArg (_ ≫ ·) h6

/-- `alternatingHomologyIso` as a natural isomorphism. -/
def alternatingHomologyNatIso (q : ℕ) :
    alternatingCechFunctor fam ⋙ HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor _ _ (q + 1) ≅
      (cechFunctor.{u} fam ⋙ HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor _ _ (q + 2)) ⋙
        forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (fun M ↦ alternatingHomologyIso fam M q)
    (fun g ↦ alternatingHomologyIso_naturality fam g q)

/-! ### Assembling the comparison -/

/-- **Sheaf cohomology on `U`, above degree zero, is the cohomology of the Čech cone.** -/
def hfunctorComplementTildeIsoSucc (q : ℕ) :
    complementTildeFunctor A I ⋙
        Hfunctor (complementZeroLocus A I : Scheme).ringCatSheaf ⊤ (q + 1) ≅
      complementCohomologyFunctor fam ((q : ℤ) + 1) ⋙ forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  hfunctorComplementTildeIsoSpec I (q + 1) ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerLeft (associatedSheafFunctor A)
      (hfunctorIsoRightDerivedEvaluation I (q + 1) ≪≫
        rightDerivedEvaluationIsoRightDerivedPlus I (q + 1) ≪≫
        Functor.isoWhiskerRight (rightDerivedPlusIsoDerivedGlobalSections I (q + 1)) _) ≪≫
    (Functor.associator _ _ _).symm ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerRight (cechCohomologyNatIsoCohomology fam I hIf (q + 1)).symm _ ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerRight (cechPlusHomologyNatIso fam I hIf (q + 1)) _ ≪≫
    sliceHomologyIsoAlternating fam I hIf (q + 1) ≪≫
    alternatingHomologyNatIso fam q ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerRight (complementCohomologyIsoCechHomology fam q).symm _

/-- **Sheaf cohomology on `U` in degree zero is the cohomology of the Čech cone**: both are the
sections of `M̃` on `U`. -/
def hfunctorComplementTildeIsoZero (hI : I.FG) :
    complementTildeFunctor A I ⋙ Hfunctor (complementZeroLocus A I : Scheme).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 0 ≅
      complementCohomologyFunctor fam 0 ⋙ forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  Functor.isoWhiskerLeft _ (HzeroIso (complementZeroLocus A I : Scheme).ringCatSheaf ⊤) ≪≫
    NatIso.ofComponents
      (fun M ↦ ((cechLocalizationTriangleData.{u} fam I hI hIf).sectionsIso M).symm.toAddEquiv
        |>.toAddCommGrpIso)
      (fun {M N} g ↦ by
        ext x
        apply ((cechLocalizationTriangleData.{u} fam I hI hIf).sectionsIso N).injective
        have h := (cechLocalizationTriangleData.{u} fam I hI hIf).sectionsIso_naturality g
          (((cechLocalizationTriangleData.{u} fam I hI hIf).sectionsIso M).symm x)
        refine (LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply _ _).trans ?_
        refine Eq.trans ?_ (h.trans (congrArg _ (LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply _ x))).symm
        exact congrArg (fun φ : associatedAbPresheaf M ⟶ associatedAbPresheaf N ↦
            ConcreteCategory.hom (φ.app (op ((complementZeroLocus A I).ι ''ᵁ ⊤))) x)
          (Koszul.associatedAbPresheafMap_eq_tilde g).symm)

/-- **The Čech cone model of `H^p(U, -)` is sheaf cohomology, naturally in the module.** For
`U = Spec A ∖ V(I)` with `I` generated by the finite family `fam`, the cohomology group
`H^p(U, M̃|U)` of [Stacks, Tag 01E3] on the open subscheme `U` is, as a functor of the `A`-module
`M` with values in abelian groups, isomorphic to `Stacks.Algebraization.complementCohomologyFunctor
fam p`, the degree-`p` cohomology of the cone of the Čech augmentation. -/
def hfunctorComplementTildeIso (hI : I.FG) : (p : ℕ) →
    complementTildeFunctor A I ⋙ Hfunctor (complementZeroLocus A I : Scheme).ringCatSheaf ⊤ p ≅
      complementCohomologyFunctor fam (p : ℤ) ⋙ forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}
  | 0 => hfunctorComplementTildeIsoZero fam I hIf hI
  | q + 1 => hfunctorComplementTildeIsoSucc fam I hIf q ≪≫
      Functor.isoWhiskerRight (eqToIso (congrArg (complementCohomologyFunctor fam)
        (Nat.cast_succ q).symm)) _

end Stacks.Algebraization.ComplementSheafComparison

